            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 13 changed paths. The change adds a regex location check (CheckLocations) applied only in Service.Record after Parse, so newly recorded replies are validated while stored results still parse.",
              "The regex is anchored and linear (RE2 in Go), so there is no ReDoS. The input is already bounded by the 1 MiB reply limit.",
              "The check only tightens validation on untrusted reviewer output and refuses malformed replies before anything is stored. No new file, path, command or network access is introduced, and no secrets or dependencies are touched.",
              "The location string is only quoted in an error message, which is truncated when re-asked (1024 bytes). The change gives no exploitable data exposure, authorization bypass or data loss.",
              "Docs and usage text updates match the behavior."
            ]
          }
        }
